Original commit body from 1949014a910ad84db37f7c494714bdac316be0e8:

The sketch's Tests line changed between runs on identical files (thc:
"2717 test files · vitest" on one cold run, "2717 test files" on the
next). _analyze_test_files built its glob list with list(<set>) --
per-process str-hash order -- find_files yields pattern by pattern, and
frameworks were detected from the FIRST 20 test files of that order. So
whether any extension/test/*.test.js landed in the sample depended on the
hash salt. ExUnit was never named because no pattern existed for it.

- Globs are sorted, and detection no longer depends on walk order at all:
  _sample_test_files_for_frameworks deals a budget of 200 files
  round-robin across sorted (extension, top-level dir) strata and spreads
  picks evenly within each, so a minority sub-project is always read.
- Repo-root runner config names frameworks used through globals
  (test/test_helper.exs ExUnit.start, vitest/jest config, pytest.ini /
  conftest.py / [tool.pytest...] / [tool:pytest] / [pytest], .rspec).
- New patterns: ExUnit (ExUnit.Case/CaseTemplate/start, and app case
  templates like `use MyAppWeb.ConnCase`), XCTest, swift-testing, xunit,
  nunit, mstest, phpunit, kotlin.test, googletest, catch2, dart test,
  flutter_test, node:test, playwright, scalatest, munit, hspec, tasty,
  clojure.test, julia Test, Rails minitest. Go grouped
  `import ( ... "testing" )` and Rust #[tokio::test] now match.
- Frameworks are listed case-insensitively sorted.

Same defect class (set/hash order reaching output), fixed here:
- Configuration section: CONFIG_FILES = list({...}) and the
  INTERESTING_DEPS / go / gem sets were iterated unordered, so root
  manifest lines swapped between runs (thc: package.json vs mix.exs) and
  the line cap made WHICH manifests appear vary; license globs sorted.
- profile: --frameworks all emitted list(<set>).
- Limits.merge: skipped_languages via list(set(...)).
- sketch_embeddings._extract_file_samples seeded its RNG with
  hash(str(path)) (salted per process); now zlib.crc32.

Evidence: thc cold sketches, two runs each, Tests line identical:
"2717 test files · ExUnit, node:test, vitest".

